<cm:compliance-check-name>19.7.4.2 Ensure &apos;Notify antivirus programs when opening attachments&apos; is set to &apos;Enabled&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>ac06acbb26dac7c785e2c62fb9d1ea18d5189d2c690c431d13f8f1af8f36d09e</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>Non-compliant items:
  HKU\S-1-5-21-2864493588-2528942772-2145745040-1000\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Attachments -</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>3</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>088f43a9b9</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting manages the behavior for notifying registered antivirus programs. If multiple programs are registered, they will all be notified.

The recommended state for this setting is: Enabled.

Note: An updated antivirus program must be installed for this policy setting to function properly.

Rationale:

Antivirus programs that do not perform on-access checks may not be able to scan downloaded files.

Impact:

Windows tells the registered antivirus program(s) to scan the file when a user opens a file attachment. If the antivirus program fails, the attachment is blocked from being opened.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>3d09cf28abdd8375ab2a427b495c45179b1ec4d95c58cc0903036b04287fdaa1</cm:compliance-informational-id>
