<cm:compliance-check-name>18.10.89.1.2 Ensure &apos;Allow unencrypted traffic&apos; is set to &apos;Disabled&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>06ed4288c77468f76e53ec760d2f92ada8601d84d6d82585f48005acb864ad64</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>NULL</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>0</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>fa9918db81</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting allows you to manage whether the Windows Remote Management (WinRM) client sends and receives unencrypted messages over the network.

The recommended state for this setting is: Disabled.

Rationale:

Encrypting WinRM network traffic reduces the risk of an attacker viewing or modifying WinRM messages as they transit the network.

Impact:

None - this is the default behavior.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
