<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>2.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>18.10.59.6 Ensure &apos;Allow search and Cortana to use location&apos; is set to &apos;Disabled&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>453742417ff256e532d14284e4115d6a0c000998ae7d602d9b452247c3b57709</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>NULL</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>0</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>f7a08ffb28</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting specifies whether search and Cortana can provide location aware search and Cortana results.

The recommended state for this setting is: Disabled.

Rationale:

In an enterprise managed environment, allowing Cortana and Search to have access to location data is unnecessary. Organizations likely do not want this information shared out.

Impact:

Search and Cortana will not have access to location information.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>fb8e870075977fc0ee72d7924ee011fe9f94d8d3529fc8bcaac52e5637776cfa</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-53|CM-6,800-53|CM-7,800-53r5|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-7,CSCv7|9.2,CSCv8|4.8,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,ITSG-33|CM-7,LEVEL|1A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Disabled:

Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\Windows Components\Search\Allow search and Cortana to use location

Note: This Group Policy path may not exist by default. It is provided by the Group Policy template Search.admx/adml that is included with the Microsoft Windows 10 RTM (Release 1507) Administrative Templates (or newer).

Default Value:

Enabled. (Search and Cortana can access location information.)</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Microsoft Windows 10 Benchmark L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>3e11b8aa418ac8f85c670d53951d173ca598427819d12bad8b93a8433cad3be3</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/12412</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>453742417ff256e532d14284e4115d6a0c000998ae7d602d9b452247c3b57709</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
