<cm:compliance-check-name>18.10.57.3.11.1 Ensure &apos;Do not delete temp folders upon exit&apos; is set to &apos;Disabled&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>98dfee3da1c91c8960ef19070476ee392181abc88c56282fb6682ed578dcae4a</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>NULL</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>1</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>cb9151e476</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting specifies whether Remote Desktop Services retains a user&apos;s per-session temporary folders at logoff.

The recommended state for this setting is: Disabled.

Rationale:

Sensitive information could be contained inside the temporary folders and visible to other administrators that log into the system.

Impact:

None - this is the default behavior.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>513ed45ac7cba4e99e27978f89281edafbdc7e7f659906b0583620b48b53718f</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-53|AU-11,800-53|SI-12,800-53r5|AU-11,800-53r5|SI-12,CSCv7|9.2,CSCv8|3.4,CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-11,ITSG-33|SI-12,ITSG-33|SI-12a.,LEVEL|1A,NESA|M5.2.3,NESA|M5.2.4,NESA|M5.3.1,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|DR1,NIAv2|DR1a,NIAv2|DR1b,NIAv2|DR1c,NIAv2|DR2,NIAv2|DR3,NIAv2|DR4,NIAv2|DR5,NIAv2|DR6,NIAv2|SM7,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|3.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.7,PCI-DSSv4.0|3.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.5.1,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Disabled:

Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\Windows Components\Remote Desktop Services\Remote Desktop Session Host\Temporary Folders\Do not delete temp folders upon exit

Note: This Group Policy path is provided by the Group Policy template TerminalServer.admx/adml that is included with all versions of the Microsoft Windows Administrative Templates.

Note #2: In older Microsoft Windows Administrative Templates, this setting was named Do not delete temp folder upon exit, but it was renamed starting with the Windows 8.0 &amp; Server 2012 (non-R2) Administrative Templates.

Default Value:

Disabled. (Temporary folders are deleted when a user logs off.)</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Microsoft Windows 10 Benchmark L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>0f088ec4e8afadaf00e21991d5c816158f5850b0fafd222b7d464ae118195110</cm:compliance-control-id>
