<cm:compliance-check-name>18.10.43.13.2 Ensure &apos;Turn on e-mail scanning&apos; is set to &apos;Enabled&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>714af1d1dade3de502ff3c9c7a2776308d3180f03c15c228620b03f306cd52f0</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>NULL</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>0</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>9fe202eccf</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting allows you to configure e-mail scanning. When e-mail scanning is enabled, the engine will parse the mailbox and mail files, according to their specific format, in order to analyze the mail bodies and attachments. Several e-mail formats are currently supported, for example: pst (Outlook), dbx, mbx, mime (Outlook Express), binhex (Mac).

The recommended state for this setting is: Enabled.

Rationale:

Incoming e-mails should be scanned by an antivirus solution such as Microsoft Defender Antivirus, as email attachments are a commonly used attack vector to infiltrate computers with malicious software.

Impact:

E-mail scanning by Microsoft Defender Antivirus will be enabled.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>9e6e74aff615934e193bcaa13637a3f11a56c60370be4988598c9dfd174bd158</cm:compliance-informational-id>
