<cm:compliance-check-name>18.6.4.1 Ensure &apos;Configure NetBIOS settings&apos; is set to &apos;Enabled: Disable NetBIOS name resolution on public networks&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>9900aee505d0e385c6b093570f8b31be84ec0ac0841107456cbede28b52ff8d0</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>NULL</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>2</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>f72869a6c3</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting specifies if the Domain Name System (DNS) client will perform name resolution over Network Basic Input/Output System (NetBIOS). NetBIOS is a legacy name resolution method for internal Microsoft networking that predates the use of DNS for that purpose (pre-Active Directory). Some legacy applications still require the use of NetBIOS for full functionality.

The recommended state for this setting is: Enabled: Disable NetBIOS name resolution on public networks. Configuring this setting to Enabled: Disable NetBIOS name resolution also conforms to the benchmark.

Rationale:

NetBIOS does not perform authentication and can allow remote attackers to cause a denial of service by sending spoofed Name Conflicts or Name Release datagrams. This is also known as &apos;NetBIOS Name Server Protocol Spoofing&apos;. Preventing the use of NetBIOS on public networks reduces the attack surface.

Impact:

None - this is the default behavior.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>a9eeeb8c906e2db89210f5cab7e31d40f4b451c902cd7a2765649719acad9758</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|1A,NESA|T3.2.1,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Enabled: Disable NetBIOS name resolution on public networks:

Computer Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\Network\DNS Client\Configure NetBIOS settings

Default Value:

Enabled. (The DNS client will disable NetBIOS name resolution on public networks.)</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Microsoft Windows 10 Benchmark L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>5936e4b0f8749013626a66793728a477a336646b1446d49b2251ae8ab1c27002</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/12412</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>9900aee505d0e385c6b093570f8b31be84ec0ac0841107456cbede28b52ff8d0</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
