<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>2.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>9.3.2 Ensure &apos;Windows Firewall: Public: Inbound connections&apos; is set to &apos;Block (default)&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>55e5367dab29d5885984e91de3d93e9fa47213fd2442c15937b0432b0d12c729</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>NULL</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>1</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>28f6a37ce7</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This setting determines the behavior for inbound connections that do not match an inbound firewall rule.

The recommended state for this setting is: Block (default).

Rationale:

If the firewall allows all traffic to access the system then an attacker may be more easily able to remotely exploit a weakness in a network service.

Impact:

None - this is the default behavior.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>eb4279d809b716c6ab8c72734c483cfad11669b374627e3f7583ce6cc7d0c1cf</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.13.1,800-171|3.13.5,800-171|3.13.6,800-53|SC-7,800-53|SC-7(5),800-53r5|SC-7,800-53r5|SC-7(5),CN-L3|7.1.2.2(c),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(j),CSCv7|9.4,CSCv7|11.2,CSCv8|4.5,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|PR.AC-5,CSF|PR.DS-5,CSF|PR.PT-4,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO/IEC-27001|A.13.1.3,ITSG-33|SC-7,ITSG-33|SC-7(5),LEVEL|1A,NESA|T4.5.4,NIAv2|GS1,NIAv2|GS2a,NIAv2|GS2b,NIAv2|GS7b,NIAv2|NS25,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.3,PCI-DSSv4.0|1.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|1.4.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,TBA-FIISB|43.1</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Block (default):

Computer Configuration\Policies\Windows Settings\Security Settings\Windows Firewall with Advanced Security\Windows Firewall with Advanced Security\Windows Firewall Properties\Public Profile\Inbound connections

Default Value:

Block (default). (The Windows Firewall with Advanced Security will block all inbound connections that do not match an inbound firewall rule in this profile.)</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Microsoft Windows 10 Benchmark L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
