<cm:compliance-check-name>5.36 Ensure &apos;Windows Media Player Network Sharing Service (WMPNetworkSvc)&apos; is set to &apos;Disabled&apos; or &apos;Not Installed&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>48065587e286c7b300cf06380c995f7f58bc8aaa838261435d745f4cd929c215</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>3</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>4</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>437c7f7136</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>Shares Windows Media Player libraries to other networked players and media devices using Universal Plug and Play.

The recommended state for this setting is: Disabled or Not Installed.

Rationale:

Network sharing of media from Media Player has no place in an enterprise managed environment.

Impact:

Windows Media Player libraries will not be shared over the network to other devices and systems.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>c069667581fb8a473ea054acd15b9fe86843bafbd12da753ba87a2b987255bf8</cm:compliance-informational-id>
