<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>PASSED</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>374edc0aee</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>Detects other Infrared devices that are in range and launches the file transfer application.

The recommended state for this setting is: Disabled or Not Installed.

Rationale:

Infrared connections can potentially be a source of data compromise - especially via the automatic &apos;file transfer application&apos; functionality. Enterprise-managed systems should utilize a more secure method of connection than infrared.

Impact:

Infrared file transfers will be prevented from working.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>370b66d019d2b80c7c9d818453861648919de83aa1bda557601f8e31998c591d</cm:compliance-informational-id>
