<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>&apos;Administrators&apos;</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>240107ae57</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This policy setting allows users to change the size of the pagefile. By making the pagefile extremely large or extremely small, an attacker could easily affect the performance of a compromised computer.

The recommended state for this setting is: Administrators.

Rationale:

Users who can change the page file size could make it extremely small or move the file to a highly fragmented storage volume, which could cause reduced computer performance.

Impact:

None - this is the default behavior.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>884d23c9eaecc54f1611edd2e99eaedba29def96b49798e0738f747b9e1815ab</cm:compliance-informational-id>
