<cm:compliance-check-name>2.2.9 Ensure &apos;Change the time zone&apos; is set to &apos;Administrators, LOCAL SERVICE, Users&apos;</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>64f72de818f8cdd6e1ccb834cb1cc08e9b150708303eda553ba93b44e416d4f4</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>&apos;users&apos; &amp;&amp; &apos;administrators&apos; &amp;&amp; &apos;local service&apos;</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_MS_Windows_10_Enterprise_Level_1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>&apos;Administrators&apos; &amp;&amp; &apos;LOCAL SERVICE&apos; &amp;&amp; &apos;Users&apos;</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>c265fdd9a9</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-info>This setting determines which users can change the time zone of the computer. This ability holds no great danger for the computer and may be useful for mobile workers.

The recommended state for this setting is: Administrators, LOCAL SERVICE, Users.

Rationale:

Changing the time zone represents little vulnerability because the system time is not affected. This setting merely enables users to display their preferred time zone while being synchronized with Domain Controllers in different time zones.

Impact:

None - this is the default behavior.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>64ef2fd2f52c80ba51777fc10109e17dc88ab3f84b28ae49ddefa8e688010038</cm:compliance-informational-id>
