<cm:compliance-check-name>5.2.19 Ensure SSH warning banner is configured</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>a6e4625da0d41bec571395f1077acec8715afb239c5aee32dc57f8e5235e6de1</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The file &quot;/etc/ssh/sshd_config&quot; does not contain &quot;^[\s]*Banner[\s]&quot;</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>expect: ^[\s]*Banner[\s]+/etc/issue.net[\s]*$
file: /etc/ssh/sshd_config
regex: ^[\s]*Banner[\s]
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>0c8558b877</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The Banner parameter specifies a file whose contents must be sent to the remote user
before authentication is permitted. By default, no banner is displayed.

Rationale:

Banners are used to warn connecting users of the particular site&apos;s policy regarding
connection. Presenting a warning message prior to the normal user login may assist the
prosecution of trespassers on the computer system.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>2b4252b1e7e7d3a731211f6159161ff78aa9e6119c7684616fa144642f7e74b3</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|5.1,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Edit the /etc/ssh/sshd_config file to set the parameter as follows:

Banner /etc/issue.net</cm:compliance-solution>
