<cm:compliance-check-name>5.1.3 Ensure permissions on /etc/cron.hourly are configured</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>fc8cbf17757abe385c4bc36191e64950fbbb1675f76d6ab720fcf83e4ca509b8</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The file /etc/cron.hourly with fmode owner: root group: root mode: 0755 uid: 0 gid: 0 uneven permissions : FALSE  does not match the policy value owner: root group: root mask: 077 uneven permissions : FALSE 

/etc/cron.hourly</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>file: /etc/cron.hourly
group: root
mask: 077
owner: root
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>36c4468b96</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>This directory contains system cron jobs that need to run on an hourly basis. The files in
this directory cannot be manipulated by the crontab command, but are instead edited by
system administrators using a text editor. The commands below restrict read/write and
search access to user and group root, preventing regular users from accessing this
directory.

Rationale:

Granting write access to this directory for non-privileged users could provide them the
means for gaining unauthorized elevated privileges. Granting read access to this directory
could give an unprivileged user insight in how to gain elevated privileges or circumvent
auditing controls.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>d845226f17c81ce55a87cef45dc64ff8d47922b16f4c5fae93067c7685ff594e</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|5.1,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Run the following commands to set ownership and permissions on /etc/cron.hourly :

# chown root:root /etc/cron.hourly
# chmod og-rwx /etc/cron.hourly</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>ce92eb4a29e6e0136cb02e6cf9b8bbc49720ea7f983931eb9633fe8a359c84b1</cm:compliance-control-id>
