<cm:compliance-check-name>4.2.2.3 Ensure journald is configured to write logfiles to persistent disk</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>9426d5f5534b0ed03569ee59b0cc3aa52f80367cf840b7bc96cdfb91fd25f69a</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The file &quot;/etc/systemd/journald.conf&quot; does not contain &quot;^[\s]*Storage=persistent&quot;</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>expect: ^[\s]*Storage=persistent
file: /etc/systemd/journald.conf
regex: ^[\s]*Storage=persistent
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>89dca42378</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Data from journald may be stored in volatile memory or persisted locally on the server.
Logs in memory will be lost upon a system reboot. By persisting logs to local disk on the
server they are protected from loss.

Rationale:

Writing log data to disk will provide the ability to forensically reconstruct events which
may have impacted the operations or security of a system even after a system crash or
reboot.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>9ea18d8fdfcda15af7cb8ce755685b571fd844387b822eca856e2d2994d78a42</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-53|AU-3,800-53|AU-12,800-53r5|AU-3,800-53r5|AU-12,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.2.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(b),CSCv6|6.2,CSCv7|6.2,CSCv7|6.3,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|DE.CM-7,CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-3,ITSG-33|AU-12,LEVEL|1S,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|AM34a,NIAv2|AM34b,NIAv2|AM34c,NIAv2|AM34d,NIAv2|AM34e,NIAv2|AM34f,NIAv2|AM34g,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.4,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Edit the /etc/systemd/journald.conf file and add the following line:

Storage=persistent</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>0493b877e08e297563fc8763d68da259bc2104f28610ca854753dac83a5d3001</cm:compliance-control-id>
