<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>2.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>4.2.2.2 Ensure journald is configured to compress large log files</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>485908b6fd8eaff08d160273e87e0db0c1da829819850e25b6539f735a7f1af7</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The file &quot;/etc/systemd/journald.conf&quot; does not contain &quot;^[\s]*Compress=yes&quot;</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>expect: ^[\s]*Compress=yes
file: /etc/systemd/journald.conf
regex: ^[\s]*Compress=yes
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>3b491f07ba</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The journald system includes the capability of compressing overly large files to avoid filling
up the system with logs or making the logs unmanageably large.

Rationale:

Uncompressed large files may unexpectedly fill a filesystem leading to resource
unavailability. Compressing logs prior to write can prevent sudden, unexpected filesystem
impacts.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>2ab2504d05ca72b72c55fb2afbd904cc615bae6773a839b281dc51d0f68f9d37</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-53|AU-4,800-53r5|AU-4,CSCv6|6.2,CSCv7|6.4,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-4,LEVEL|1S,NESA|T3.3.1,NESA|T3.6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Edit the /etc/systemd/journald.conf file and add the following line:

Compress=yes</cm:compliance-solution>
