<cm:compliance-check-name>3.3.5 Ensure permissions on /etc/hosts.deny are configured</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>3911c3209daaf8e5bb8966039bfb9654600693b13f24929f85189911293dbdca</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>No files found: /etc/hosts.deny</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>file: /etc/hosts.deny
group: root
mask: 133
owner: root
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>dc963787c0</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The /etc/hosts.deny file contains network information that is used by many system
applications and therefore must be readable for these applications to operate.

Rationale:

It is critical to ensure that the /etc/hosts.deny file is protected from unauthorized write
access. Although it is protected by default, the file permissions could be changed either
inadvertently or through malicious actions.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>42f35ff51f50319e8dc874fafd23c144f1defdf4bf9c7314f0e6163bfb067bb0</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|5.1,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Run the following commands to set permissions on /etc/hosts.deny :

# chown root:root /etc/hosts.deny
# chmod 644 /etc/hosts.deny</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>49c68fe35616964589a049ce79c744011c4a987ea66ea578dbe54d2060aca1cb</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>3911c3209daaf8e5bb8966039bfb9654600693b13f24929f85189911293dbdca</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
