<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>2.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>3.3.3 Ensure /etc/hosts.deny is configured</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>87f8b9a84dc33973d3a7851dde774ca2a7d5e84fe0e0e4d17ccfddaf278e298c</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>No files found: /etc/hosts.deny</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>expect: ^[\s]*ALL:[\s\t]*ALL$
file: /etc/hosts.deny
regex: ^[\s]*ALL[\s]*:
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>c6e2f238e4</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The /etc/hosts.deny file specifies which IP addresses are not permitted to connect to the
host. It is intended to be used in conjunction with the /etc/hosts.allow file.

Rationale:

The /etc/hosts.deny file serves as a failsafe so that any host not specified in
/etc/hosts.allow is denied access to the system.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>c445ac124654ea5ff96a208a24b1d90229e8f868e91e62c36770a74bf19a44df</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.13.1,800-53|SC-7(12),800-53r5|SC-7(12),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(j),CSCv6|9.2,CSCv7|9.4,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|PR.AC-5,CSF|PR.DS-5,CSF|PR.PT-4,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO/IEC-27001|A.13.1.3,ITSG-33|SC-7(12),LEVEL|1NS,NESA|T4.5.4,NIAv2|AM38,NIAv2|SS13d,NIAv2|SS26,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.4,PCI-DSSv4.0|1.5.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,TBA-FIISB|43.1</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Run the following command to create /etc/hosts.deny:

# echo &quot;ALL: ALL&quot; &gt;&gt; /etc/hosts.deny

Notes:

Contents of the /etc/hosts.deny file may include additional options depending on your
network configuration.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>d608950e27ebfa18c9a131df5a91fba843ed274cc34374fbe29b746098c63298</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>87f8b9a84dc33973d3a7851dde774ca2a7d5e84fe0e0e4d17ccfddaf278e298c</cm:compliance-full-id>
