attacker as opposed to a valid system.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>f01e4a489945ea5ee738c673b3daf53e4988526159afcd112866eeaf0af856da</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|11,CSCv6|3,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Set the following parameters in /etc/sysctl.conf or a /etc/sysctl.d/* file:

net.ipv4.conf.all.send_redirects = 0
net.ipv4.conf.default.send_redirects = 0

Run the following commands to set the active kernel parameters:

# sysctl -w net.ipv4.conf.all.send_redirects=0
# sysctl -w net.ipv4.conf.default.send_redirects=0
# sysctl -w net.ipv4.route.flush=1</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>147565108f10761033e23fdb90a321472c5fb0836232a4dd8fae32bd1f5ee376</cm:compliance-control-id>
