<cm:compliance-check-name>1.3.2 Ensure filesystem integrity is regularly checked</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>28d3c4bfcf30f4347f924c67f13dff461eddc4219f09e8687ba227a429c365c2</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The command &apos;crontab -l&apos; returned : 

no crontab for root</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>cmd: crontab -l
expect: ^(\d{1,2}|\*|[\s]+){9,}[\s]+(root)?[\s]*/usr/[s]?bin/aide[\s]+--check[\s]*(.*)$
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>565fd690b7</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Periodic checking of the filesystem integrity is needed to detect changes to the filesystem.

Rationale:

Periodic file checking allows the system administrator to determine on a regular basis if
critical files have been changed in an unauthorized fashion.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>80ff31790b87f22eaf05694a8762270ecfd8323edf154019a6682b8fa38af318</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-53|AU-3,800-53r5|AU-3,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.2.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(b),CSCv6|3.5,CSCv7|14.9,CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-3,LEVEL|1S,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|AM34a,NIAv2|AM34b,NIAv2|AM34c,NIAv2|AM34d,NIAv2|AM34e,NIAv2|AM34f,NIAv2|AM34g,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.4,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.2.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Run the following commands:

# cp ./config/aidecheck.service /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.service
# cp ./config/aidecheck.timer /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.timer
# chmod 0644 /etc/systemd/system/aidecheck.*
# systemctl reenable aidecheck.timer
# systemctl restart aidecheck.timer
# systemctl daemon-reload

or
Run the following command:

# crontab -u root -e

Add the following line to the crontab:

0 5 * * * /usr/sbin/aide --check</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>9c22a2fcbf63c1617787c4b081056c2e43114182b0539b9861d0558723856744</cm:compliance-control-id>
