<cm:compliance-check-name>1.1.14 Ensure nodev option set on /home partition</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>889797401e943981a8724aa05271c859804572da26f9653e43f98fe537d52a32</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The command &apos;mount | grep &apos;on /home &apos;&apos; did not return any result</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>cmd: mount | grep &apos;on /home &apos;
expect: nodev
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>a06cf5cb45</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The nodev mount option specifies that the filesystem cannot contain special devices.

Rationale:

Since the user partitions are not intended to support devices, set this option to ensure that
users cannot attempt to create block or character special devices.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>58d581039ac6d77e3c43ebf3d8db3a6a335cdd2a80e3246042b1d7d78bc09edf</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|13,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Edit the /etc/fstab file and add nodev to the fourth field (mounting options) for the /home
partition. See the fstab(5) manual page for more information.

# mount -o remount,nodev /home

Notes:

The actions in this recommendation refer to the /homepartition, which is the default user
partition that is defined in many distributions. If you have created other user partitions, it
is recommended that the Remediation and Audit steps be applied to these partitions as
well.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>a5abcbe8ad69a96f495446d2c10bfa1c02deb59cc0bab2d1f10382483eddafdb</cm:compliance-control-id>
