<cm:compliance-check-id>8a401030576c00b691546ab626f87b4382069319ab84df29bec83dcf2dfd2770</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The command &apos;modprobe -n -v squashfs | awk &apos;{print} END {if (NR == 0) print &quot;fail&quot;}&apos;&apos; returned : 

insmod /lib/modules/4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64/kernel/fs/squashfs/squashfs.ko.xz</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>cmd: modprobe -n -v squashfs | awk &apos;{print} END {if (NR == 0) print &quot;fail&quot;}&apos;
expect: install /bin/true
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>7aac8921b5</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The squashfs filesystem type is a compressed read-only Linux filesystem embedded in
small footprint systems (similar to cramfs ). A squashfs image can be used without having
to first decompress the image.

Rationale:

Removing support for unneeded filesystem types reduces the local attack surface of the
system. If this filesystem type is not needed, disable it.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>b790b7f54518dfb3785c55c626cdf156c6233736510362737237f07ecf954dd5</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|13,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Edit or create a file in the /etc/modprobe.d/ directory ending in .conf
Example: vim /etc/modprobe.d/squashfs.conf
and add the following line:

install squashfs /bin/true

Run the following command to unload the squashfs module:

# rmmod squashfs</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>d6752a154de3439c1369467bc9b43102c77f1eb74e3d080f2ab70424836c8ee5</cm:compliance-control-id>
