<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>2.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>6.2.19 Ensure no duplicate group names exist</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>87d7be9be33f4b2abfca48f3fe5090ddfa94814e91b2c3137414f93e4bcd69b6</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>No issues found.</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>name: group_duplicate_name
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>1fbc91d722</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Although the groupadd program will not let you create a duplicate group name, it is
possible for an administrator to manually edit the /etc/group file and change the group
name.

Rationale:

If a group is assigned a duplicate group name, it will create and have access to files with the
first GID for that group in /etc/group . Effectively, the GID is shared, which is a security
problem.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>a6a322835bc3d132cd593d602e8b23c120f2bb668f6e79be02b913bbeaccce87</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.1.1,800-53|AC-2,800-53r5|AC-2,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(d),CSCv6|16,CSCv7|16,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF|PR.AC-4,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.2.1,ITSG-33|AC-2,LEVEL|1S,NIAv2|AM28,NIAv2|NS5j,NIAv2|SS14e,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,QCSC-v1|15.2</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Based on the results of the audit script, establish unique names for the user groups. File
group ownerships will automatically reflect the change as long as the groups have unique
GIDs.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>b23e3d0331cb841512554fce5e298f94f3686a74d4f5c965f1250ad9a4500add</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>87d7be9be33f4b2abfca48f3fe5090ddfa94814e91b2c3137414f93e4bcd69b6</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
