<cm:compliance-check-name>6.2.11 Ensure no users have .forward files</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>f3d43a303bedee1a935fde0a52553dd5e739e1d5839002edea5accf59ff104c7</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The command &apos;cat /etc/passwd | egrep -v &apos;^(root|halt|sync|shutdown)&apos; | awk -F: &apos;($7 !~ &quot;(/usr)?/sbin/nologin&quot; &amp;&amp; $7 != &quot;/bin/false&quot;) { print $1 &quot; &quot; $6 }&apos; | while read user dir; do if [ ! -d &quot;$dir&quot; ]; then echo &quot;The home directory ($dir) of user $user does not exist.&quot;; else if [ ! -h &quot;$dir/.forward&quot; -a -f &quot;$dir/.forward&quot; ]; then echo &quot;.forward file $dir/.forward exists&quot;; fi; fi; done | awk &apos;{ print } END { if (NR==0) print &quot;No users have forward files&quot; }&apos;&apos; returned : 

No users have forward files</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>cmd: cat /etc/passwd | egrep -v &apos;^(root|halt|sync|shutdown)&apos; | awk -F: &apos;($7 !~ &quot;(/usr)?/sbin/nologin&quot; &amp;&amp; $7 != &quot;/bin/false&quot;) { print $1 &quot; &quot; $6 }&apos; | while read user dir; do if [ ! -d &quot;$dir&quot; ]; then echo &quot;The home directory ($dir) of user $user does not exist.&quot;; else if [ ! -h &quot;$dir/.forward&quot; -a -f &quot;$dir/.forward&quot; ]; then echo &quot;.forward file $dir/.forward exists&quot;; fi; fi; done | awk &apos;{ print } END { if (NR==0) print &quot;No users have forward files&quot; }&apos;
expect: No users have forward files
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>85e7c2e0d7</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The .forward file specifies an email address to forward the user&apos;s mail to.

Rationale:

Use of the .forward file poses a security risk in that sensitive data may be inadvertently
transferred outside the organization. The .forward file also poses a risk as it can be used to
execute commands that may perform unintended actions.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>3015bc5701e0d16bfaa967c9c50fbc71ce592f3b05e0bfe9b526bd37681972be</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|7,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Making global modifications to users&apos; files without alerting the user community can result
in unexpected outages and unhappy users. Therefore, it is recommended that a monitoring
policy be established to report user .forward files and determine the action to be taken in
accordance with site policy.

Notes:

On some distributions the /sbin/nologin should be replaced with /usr/sbin/nologin.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>caa97507f83e5c4d8299048849d90c2c988139503172b9ccfebfafb87a261671</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>f3d43a303bedee1a935fde0a52553dd5e739e1d5839002edea5accf59ff104c7</cm:compliance-full-id>
