<cm:compliance-check-name>6.2.7 Ensure all users&apos; home directories exist</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>200cf419fc1908510df953bbf381514a72378e0a81e610a2f8cd0c93f9ef5802</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>No issues found.</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>name: active_accounts_without_home_dir
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>7d5811b86e</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Users can be defined in /etc/passwd without a home directory or with a home directory
that does not actually exist.

Rationale:

If the user&apos;s home directory does not exist or is unassigned, the user will be placed in &quot;/&quot;
and will not be able to write any files or have local environment variables set.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>29e854ba11ec3fc8cba32b0b4d06bd909a8fe9a870add4b573e90ae8d120408a</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|13,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>If any users&apos; home directories do not exist, create them and make sure the respective user
owns the directory. Users without an assigned home directory should be removed or
assigned a home directory as appropriate.

Notes:

The audit script checks all users UID 500 and above except nfsnobody. Some distributions
split at UID 1000 instead, consult your documentation and/or the UID_MIN setting in
/etc/login.defs to determine which is appropriate for you.

On some distributions the /sbin/nologin should be replaced with /usr/sbin/nologin.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>e81d9ae8ed201df2bd617476e5d45eed011b4d5fb3d5b2dee4a2b8739f8b62b8</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>200cf419fc1908510df953bbf381514a72378e0a81e610a2f8cd0c93f9ef5802</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
