<cm:compliance-check-name>6.1.12 Ensure no ungrouped files or directories exist</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>8850ee648230ba7bfe8af26b533b1d8009ce8b3f965b6d712c72a4e2e0c99e84</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>No issues found.</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>find_option: nogroup
name: find_orphan_files</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>edf41cc20c</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Sometimes when administrators delete users or groups from the system they neglect to
remove all files owned by those users or groups.

Rationale:

A new user who is assigned the deleted user&apos;s user ID or group ID may then end up
&quot;owning&quot; these files, and thus have more access on the system than was intended.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>5ed044ab5a8eb155caa56b7709a929d7bc300c9146b5590c76ec4dfb23e2cb4d</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-53|CM-7,800-53r5|CM-7,CSCv6|14,CSCv7|13.2,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,LEVEL|1S,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Locate files that are owned by users or groups not listed in the system configuration files,
and reset the ownership of these files to some active user on the system as appropriate.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>b805114fcbbe22ff4daa43f3e58c3133e351e0072adf1726ee031a3f367d430a</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>8850ee648230ba7bfe8af26b533b1d8009ce8b3f965b6d712c72a4e2e0c99e84</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
