<cm:compliance-info>The /etc/group- file contains a backup list of all the valid groups defined in the system.

Rationale:

It is critical to ensure that the /etc/group- file is protected from unauthorized access.
Although it is protected by default, the file permissions could be changed either
inadvertently or through malicious actions.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
