<cm:compliance-actual-value>The file /etc/passwd with fmode owner: root group: root mode: 0644 uid: 0 gid: 0 uneven permissions : FALSE is compliant with the policy value 

/etc/passwd</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>file: /etc/passwd
group: root
mask: 133
owner: root
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>74947d7cf9</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The /etc/passwd file contains user account information that is used by many system
utilities and therefore must be readable for these utilities to operate.

Rationale:

It is critical to ensure that the /etc/passwd file is protected from unauthorized write
access. Although it is protected by default, the file permissions could be changed either
inadvertently or through malicious actions.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>aed1ed8a5bbb6f397821eed744348676cabb05cc26dfda86be1ad64338d47745</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.5.2,800-53|IA-5,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5,800-53r5|IA-5(1),CSCv6|16.14,CSCv7|16.4,CSF|PR.AC-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ITSG-33|IA-5,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|1S,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Run the following command to set permissions on /etc/passwd :

# chown root:root /etc/passwd
# chmod 644 /etc/passwd</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>6c393772d54e225d8391dd9605a0581ed515a7b1066070f7c7f5c137ad3e260e</cm:compliance-control-id>
