<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>2.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>3.1.1 Ensure IP forwarding is disabled - sysctl ipv6</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>dc7c230b4d73cfb8bf82302cab9e740a143d230943c62bfdef538b8a9ce9794a</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The command &apos;sysctl net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding&apos; returned : 

net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding = 0</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>cmd: sysctl net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding
expect: ^[\s]*net\.ipv6\.conf\.all\.forwarding[\s]*=[\s]*0[\s]*$
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>b89054ec9f</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The net.ipv4.ip_forward and net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding flags are used to tell the
system whether it can forward packets or not.

Rationale:

Setting the flags to 0 ensures that a system with multiple interfaces (for example, a hard
proxy), will never be able to forward packets, and therefore, never serve as a router.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>2e80e1fc9c3b3b11d784d60216353a01c2e7fe10b792be7dcb5e0a06b42b3fd7</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-53|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-6,CSCv6|11,CSCv6|3,CSCv7|5.1,CSF|PR.IP-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,LEVEL|1S,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Set the following parameter in /etc/sysctl.conf or a /etc/sysctl.d/* file:

net.ipv4.ip_forward = 0
net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding = 0

Run the following commands to set the active kernel parameters:

# sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=0
# sysctl -w net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding=0
# sysctl -w net.ipv4.route.flush=1
# sysctl -w net.ipv6.route.flush=1</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>e01a44b13d9b4ff62cd7b975562da19b9e786c1627bf735300a7ed52dd66faaf</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>dc7c230b4d73cfb8bf82302cab9e740a143d230943c62bfdef538b8a9ce9794a</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
