<cm:compliance-check-name>2.3.5 Ensure LDAP client is not installed</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>ebb67c77a75e2f0035fbce17fa823ad8c03b8d22c775ffdac30584d47c5263d7</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The package &apos;openldap-clients-0.0.0-0&apos; is not installed</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>operator: lt
required: NO
rpm: openldap-clients-0.0.0-0
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>122c4139cd</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) was introduced as a replacement for
NIS/YP. It is a service that provides a method for looking up information from a central
database.

Rationale:

If the system will not need to act as an LDAP client, it is recommended that the software be
removed to reduce the potential attack surface.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>121e522456c84815867299d0ff44aeba5b90f44cacd37a1057aa701bf4811a88</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.9,800-53|CM-11,800-53r5|CM-11,CSCv6|2,CSCv7|2.6,CSF|DE.CM-3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.2,LEVEL|1S,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Uninstall openldap-clients using the appropriate package manager or manual
installation:

# yum remove openldap-clients

# apt-get remove openldap-clients

# zypper remove openldap-clients

Impact:

Removing the LDAP client will prevent or inhibit using LDAP for authentication in your
environment.

Notes:

The openldap-clients package can go by other names on some distributions. openldap2-
client, and ldap-utils are known alternative package names.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>c86a51ae8148b32b369f4b3e7c276d60814c3e0c4c4e64177a9af3ccb1104305</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>ebb67c77a75e2f0035fbce17fa823ad8c03b8d22c775ffdac30584d47c5263d7</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
