<cm:compliance-check-name>1.5.3 Ensure address space layout randomization (ASLR) is enabled</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>0866f282ddffbbdf4274c79d55e78128fe9f81c1a79360ca6ac1630e13a50a89</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The command &apos;sysctl kernel.randomize_va_space&apos; returned : 

kernel.randomize_va_space = 2</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Distribution_Independent_Linux_Server_L1_v2.0.0.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>cmd: sysctl kernel.randomize_va_space
expect: ^[\s]*kernel\.randomize_va_space[\s]*=[\s]*2[\s]*$
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>46112eb50e</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux alma.aud507.local 4.18.0-372.32.1.el8_6.x86_64 #1 SMP Tue Oct 25 05:53:57 EDT 2022 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Address space layout randomization (ASLR) is an exploit mitigation technique which
randomly arranges the address space of key data areas of a process.

Rationale:

Randomly placing virtual memory regions will make it difficult to write memory page
exploits as the memory placement will be consistently shifting.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>a68dc09e25f27136fd2acd02e461b70b986552e2bbcb86073b1cf2e3180f43fe</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-53|SC-39,800-53|SI-16,800-53r5|SC-39,800-53r5|SI-16,CSCv6|8.4,CSCv7|8.3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-16,LEVEL|1S,QCSC-v1|5.2.1</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Set the following parameter in /etc/sysctl.conf or a /etc/sysctl.d/* file:

kernel.randomize_va_space = 2

Run the following command to set the active kernel parameter:

# sysctl -w kernel.randomize_va_space=2</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Distribution Independent Linux Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>fa4a29f5c2229f02b2e7c5da4284ee26a457968f5ab4bd73420a19f0a15b9ab2</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/2420</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>0866f282ddffbbdf4274c79d55e78128fe9f81c1a79360ca6ac1630e13a50a89</cm:compliance-full-id>
</ReportItem>
