<cm:compliance-info>Single user mode is used for recovery when the system detects an issue during boot or by
manual selection from the bootloader.

Rationale:

Requiring authentication in single user mode prevents an unauthorized user from
rebooting the system into single user to gain root privileges without credentials.</cm:compliance-info>
