<cm:compliance-info>Users can be defined in /etc/passwd without a home directory or with a home directory that does not actually exist.

Rationale:

If the user&apos;s home directory does not exist or is unassigned, the user will be placed in &apos;/&apos; and will not be able to write any files or have local environment variables set.</cm:compliance-info>
