<cm:compliance-check-name>5.2.19 Ensure SSH MaxStartups is configured</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>c8f9361cbc70cc9d3918f522c7e7eb301266342a10fa5dc8ad29d2243a5c9ee7</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-actual-value>The file &quot;/etc/ssh/sshd_config&quot; does not contain &quot;^[\s]*[Mm]ax[Ss]tartups[\s]&quot;</cm:compliance-actual-value>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Ubuntu_22.04_LTS_v1.0.0_Server_L1.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>expect: ^[\s]*[Mm]ax[Ss]tartups[\s]+10:30:60[\s]*$
file: /etc/ssh/sshd_config
regex: ^[\s]*[Mm]ax[Ss]tartups[\s]
system: Linux</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>b96230e6c9</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The MaxStartups parameter specifies the maximum number of concurrent unauthenticated connections to the SSH daemon.

Rationale:

To protect a system from denial of service due to a large number of pending authentication connection attempts, use the rate limiting function of MaxStartups to protect availability of sshd logins and prevent overwhelming the daemon.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>FAILED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>9e7532b3497bbfe441f330500ffcfa62e42a7dda8d7286c556c3af720e103fa1</cm:compliance-informational-id>
