<cm:compliance-benchmark-version>1.0.0</cm:compliance-benchmark-version>
<cm:compliance-check-name>5.5.1.5 Ensure all users last password change date is in the past</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>c04040bbd30b33d25b29d97fc288430ac96ca04608aea94f6d9fb65aba030a44</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Ubuntu_22.04_LTS_v1.0.0_Server_L1.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>f17a482647</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>All users should have a password change date in the past.

Rationale:

If a users recorded password change date is in the future then they could bypass any set password expiration.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>ERROR</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>85cbb47030aafdecf78e7bbdef2925b4c1551928620740ce911b6232fd4d06fc</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.5.2,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CSCv7|4.4,CSCv8|5.2,CSF|PR.AC-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|1A,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Investigate any users with a password change date in the future and correct them. Locking the account, expiring the password, or resetting the password manually may be appropriate.</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Ubuntu Linux 22.04 LTS Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>7ea6b0a0e02d7490af18a6cfe877676962bb3ed5157b6e7e2db11c984417c445</cm:compliance-control-id>
