<cm:compliance-info>Secure ICMP redirects are the same as ICMP redirects, except they come from gateways listed on the default gateway list. It is assumed that these gateways are known to your system, and that they are likely to be secure.

Rationale:

It is still possible for even known gateways to be compromised.

Setting:

net.ipv4.conf.default.secure_redirects = 0

net.ipv4.conf.all.secure_redirects = 0

protects the system from routing table updates by possibly compromised known gateways.</cm:compliance-info>
