<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The net.ipv4.ip_forward and net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding flags are used to tell the system whether it can forward packets or not.

Rationale:

Setting:

net.ipv4.ip_forward = 0

net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding = 0

Ensures that a system with multiple interfaces (for example, a hard proxy), will never be able to forward packets, and therefore, never serve as a router.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>ERROR</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>26be541e974bffe6f4d6451fe3c6927534646234a53aa40579207e28127cf2e1</cm:compliance-informational-id>
