<cm:compliance-check-name>2.2.16 Ensure rsync service is either not installed or masked</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>7a7b95ebc4999c26b52cbc2c708d7f4e057f79a192c3c43257bc48088eb8bf5b</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Ubuntu_22.04_LTS_v1.0.0_Server_L1.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>3edb9af51f</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The rsync service can be used to synchronize files between systems over network links.

Rationale:

The rsync service presents a security risk as it uses unencrypted protocols for communication. The rsync package should be removed to reduce the attack area of the system.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>ERROR</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>4efc7b6274f6762905b70cd0b7a7ce3815a58671d063c3a90e5503cf1e30d8fd</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.4.2,800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-53|CM-6,800-53|CM-7,800-53r5|CM-6,800-53r5|CM-7,CSCv7|9.2,CSCv8|4.8,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-6,ITSG-33|CM-7,LEVEL|1A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Run the following command to remove rsync:

# apt purge rsync

OR
Run the following commands to stop and mask rsync:

# systemctl stop rsync

# systemctl mask rsync</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Ubuntu Linux 22.04 LTS Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
