<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The Network File System (NFS) is one of the first and most widely distributed file systems in the UNIX environment. It provides the ability for systems to mount file systems of other servers through the network.

Rationale:

If the system does not export NFS shares or act as an NFS client, it is recommended that these services be removed to reduce the remote attack surface.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>ERROR</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>73271c13dbcb5594cedde3b5f1e89ad362dd81a8a769024e186e1339183511fa</cm:compliance-informational-id>
