<cm:compliance-check-name>1.5.1 Ensure address space layout randomization (ASLR) is enabled - config</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>602fee120fc9e077a68114a7df646a25e0ebc7898c42078b59836ef74b2395c8</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Ubuntu_22.04_LTS_v1.0.0_Server_L1.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>ff15f2ed9b</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>Address space layout randomization (ASLR) is an exploit mitigation technique which randomly arranges the address space of key data areas of a process.

Rationale:

Randomly placing virtual memory regions will make it difficult to write memory page exploits as the memory placement will be consistently shifting.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>ERROR</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>96ba4c31b56e4dabbd380f8d1979f2a30f0bae8ffdc0a6496e35d5b93c2f8d85</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-53|SI-16,800-53r5|SI-16,CSCv7|8.3,CSCv8|10.5,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-16,LEVEL|1A</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Set the following parameter in /etc/sysctl.conf or a /etc/sysctl.d/* file:
Example:

# printf &apos;
kernel.randomize_va_space = 2
&apos; &gt;&gt; /etc/sysctl.d/60-kernel_sysctl.conf

Run the following command to set the active kernel parameter:

# sysctl -w kernel.randomize_va_space=2

Default Value:

kernel.randomize_va_space = 2</cm:compliance-solution>
<cm:compliance-benchmark-name>CIS Ubuntu Linux 22.04 LTS Server L1</cm:compliance-benchmark-name>
<cm:compliance-control-id>c78a949b9f2ccbdeef0af8bc42afb88b98beef1139f96ace7304d6c7099bc3bb</cm:compliance-control-id>
<cm:compliance-see-also>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/files/4068</cm:compliance-see-also>
<cm:compliance-full-id>602fee120fc9e077a68114a7df646a25e0ebc7898c42078b59836ef74b2395c8</cm:compliance-full-id>
