<cm:compliance-check-name>4.2.1.3 Ensure journald is configured to compress large log files</cm:compliance-check-name>
<cm:compliance-check-id>15fa67184b7824eb54d25626d080948484e1ad14f22a0f9bfdc070e2bfea8d11</cm:compliance-check-id>
<cm:compliance-source>custom</cm:compliance-source>
<cm:compliance-audit-file>CIS_Ubuntu_22.04_LTS_v1.0.0_Server_L1.audit</cm:compliance-audit-file>
<cm:compliance-policy-value>PASSED</cm:compliance-policy-value>
<cm:compliance-functional-id>374edc0aee</cm:compliance-functional-id>
<cm:compliance-uname>Linux ubuntu 5.15.0-84-generic #93-Ubuntu SMP Tue Sep 5 17:16:10 UTC 2023 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux</cm:compliance-uname>
<cm:compliance-info>The journald system includes the capability of compressing overly large files to avoid filling up the system with logs or making the logs unmanageably large.

Rationale:

Uncompressed large files may unexpectedly fill a filesystem leading to resource unavailability. Compressing logs prior to write can prevent sudden, unexpected filesystem impacts.</cm:compliance-info>
<cm:compliance-result>PASSED</cm:compliance-result>
<cm:compliance-informational-id>c797938ca04f22473d6466c388e331041d61d816cedb347036b24870b857671c</cm:compliance-informational-id>
<cm:compliance-reference>800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171|3.3.6,800-53|AU-2,800-53|AU-4,800-53|AU-7,800-53|AU-12,800-53r5|AU-2,800-53r5|AU-4,800-53r5|AU-7,800-53r5|AU-12,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(a),CSCv7|6.2,CSCv7|6.3,CSCv7|6.4,CSCv8|8.2,CSCv8|8.3,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|DE.CM-7,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF|RS.AN-3,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-2,ITSG-33|AU-4,ITSG-33|AU-7,ITSG-33|AU-12,LEVEL|1A,NESA|M1.2.2,NESA|M5.5.1,NESA|T3.3.1,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|AM7,NIAv2|AM11a,NIAv2|AM11b,NIAv2|AM11c,NIAv2|AM11d,NIAv2|AM11e,NIAv2|SS30,NIAv2|VL8,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.1,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|10.2.1,QCSC-v1|11.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4</cm:compliance-reference>
<cm:compliance-solution>Edit the /etc/systemd/journald.conf file or a file ending in .conf in /etc/systemd/journald.conf.d/ and add the following line:

Compress=yes

Restart the service:

